.IR session (2),
.IR sh-session (1),
.IR inputtest (1),
.IR pointer (3)
.SH BUGS
It reports the button's position from Tk's own
.B -actx
and
.BR -acty ,
added to the toplevel's.
If a window manager moves the window afterwards the position is stale, and the
click goes wherever it now points.
.PP
A button and a menu, which are two kinds of widget out of many.
.PP
What the menu establishes is that the movement inside a
.I drag
is tracked.
A standalone
.B move
\(em the pointer going somewhere and staying there, with no button \(em still
has no demonstration, only the same reasoning.
